From 4509bff63b91117d2847b19992fc4f4f8614d72d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PromethenDev <PromethenDev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 21:05:40 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 26/97] vulkan: asynchronous submission worker for non-swap
 submissions

The GPU command thread replayed the deferred command buffer into a
VkCommandBuffer and called vkQueueSubmit for every submission (~4 per frame),
~15% of its time in heavy seconds. Non-swap submissions now hand the recorded
stream (swapped into one of 3 spare DeferredCommandBuffers), a command buffer, a
pre-reset fence and the wait semaphores to a worker thread that records and
submits them; the command processor keeps the bookkeeping and continues with
the guest ring. Swap submissions drain the worker and stay inline, so
presentation ordering is unchanged. Blocking fence waits drain up to the awaited
submission first; non-blocking fence polls only visit fences whose submission
has been published as submitted (release after vkQueueSubmit returns), so the
command processor never touches a fence the worker is submitting. Worker errors
are observed on the command processor thread. Census: submit drain time,
[rate-census-submit] worker busy and jobs. Kill switch: WWE13_ASYNC_SUBMIT=0.

WWE 13, same-binary A/B: GPU command thread busy per draw 1.96 -> 1.84 us,
command-thread submit time 80 -> 32 ms/s; final version 1.81 us; 8 replayed
frames pixel-identical; no captures. A fence race found by independent review
(challenger) is fixed here.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
